skills-to-distribute/skills/gitnexus-*/

# PQC secrets — bundle and audit log (the .env patterns above cover
# most cases, but PQC artifacts are explicit for clarity)
secrets.bundle.json
secrets.bundle.json.bak.*
audit.log
audit.log.*
# Local pqc-sign public keys (used for verification, not for committing)
.pqc-keys/*.priv
.pqc-keys/*.sk
.agents/audit/*.priv
.agents/audit/*.sk
.agents/audit/keys/*.priv
.agents/audit/keys/*.sk
**/*.priv
**/*.sk

# Hermes / agent plan and context directories (auto-injected by
# subdirectory context discovery — never intended for git)
.hermes/
.omx/
.omo/
.omp/

# Agent COMMS live board — in-flight coordination, never committed.
# The daily team ledger .agents/comms/{date}-team.md IS committed; this sidecar is not.
# Both suffixes are ignored: `.live.txt` predates the 2026-11-12 cutover, `.live.md` is current.
# The pattern is `*.live.*`, not `*-team.live.*`: other boards use the same convention with a
# different prefix (`{date}-identity-guard.live.txt`), and the narrow form let one of those be
# committed by accident.
.agents/comms/*.live.txt
.agents/comms/*.live.md

# Multimodal RAG local vector store and runtime process PID.
# Ignored as directory *contents* rather than as a directory, so the benchmark baseline below can
# be re-included: git never descends into an ignored directory, so a `!.agents/rag/x` exception is
# inert while `.agents/rag/` itself is ignored.
.agents/rag/*
# ...except the benchmark baseline, which is the committed floor every retrieval change is
# measured against (Phase 0 of docs/rag-context-system-plan.md). It holds no secrets or vectors.
!.agents/rag/bench-baseline.json

# A nested `.agents/` created by running `ainish-context wiki --path <subdir>` from a subdirectory.
# The rules above are root-anchored, so these are NOT covered: one showed up under the context
# engine's former `src/rag/.agents/`
# carrying `audit/signer.mldsa65.priv` (a private ML-DSA-65 key) and a session PSK. Nested state is
# never a source artifact — it is engine output written to the wrong tree — so it is ignored
# wholesale, and running the engine from a subdirectory stays safe. The root `.agents/` stays tracked.
/src/context/.agents/
/skills-to-distribute/**/.agents/
/**/.agents/rag/
/**/.agents/audit/
/**/.agents/wiki/
# ...EXCEPT the root repository's own wiki vault. The rule above exists to keep a nested
# `src/context/.agents/` (which once carried a private ML-DSA-65 key) out of git. The root wiki is
# different: it is this repository's curated corpus, and from 2026-11-18 it is also where the context
# harness writes learned skills. Without this negation every such page is silently untracked and
# dies on clone — learned behaviour that does not survive a checkout is worse than none. Negating the
# root DIRECTORY (not a file pattern under it) is what makes git descend at all; the nested paths above
# stay ignored because this exception names the root exactly.
!/.agents/wiki/

# Rules auto-sync runtime artifacts (manifest and sync script ARE committed)
.agents/ainish-sync.log
.agents/.rules-sync.lock/

# Compiled native binaries (built locally via cargo or distributed wrappers)
*.exe

# Platform binaries for the retired compiled context engine. The engine is Python-only now
# (src/context/engine.py), so these are never produced — kept ignored so a stale build left on an
# older host cannot be committed into a tree that has no use for it.
bin/ainish-rag-darwin
bin/ainish-rag-linux
bin/ainish-rag-windows.exe
bin/ainish-rag.exe
bin/ainish-rag.native.exe

# Deployment smoke sandbox (created by 'ainish-coder --rules test'); never tracked.
/test/

